  "title": "The Origin of Oxygenic Photosynthesis",
  "summary": "Earth in the Archean Eon, 4,000 to 2,500 million years ago, appeared as an alien world. The planet’s crust was stabilizing, green oceans were filled with dissolved iron, and the atmosphere had negligible oxygen. Microbial life subsisted on chemical energy extracted from boiling plumes erupting miles deep in dark, hydrothermal vents, as it already had done for over a billion years.",
